[Expected Approach] Using Subarray Contribution and XOR Property - O(n) Time and O(1) SpaceEach element arr[i] (0-based index) appears in all subarrays that start at or before index i and end at or after index i. There are (i + 1) choices for the starting index (from 0 to i) and (n - i) choices for the ending index (from i to n-1), so the total number of subarrays containing arr[i] is (i + 1) * (n - i).In the XOR of all subarrays, an element only contributes if it appears an odd number of times, because XORing a number an even number of times cancels it out. Therefore, we include arr[i] in the final XOR only if both (i + 1) and (n - i) are odd, which ensures the total count is odd.
